The proposed fix is right as it stands, with one addition to cover the failed-critic log line:

const issues = critiques.flatMap((c, i) => c && Array.isArray(c.issues) ? c.issues.map(x => ({ aspect: aspects[i].key, ...x })) : [])
const failedCritics = aspects.filter((a, i) => !critiques[i]).map(a => a.key)
log(`${issues.length} issues from ${critiques.filter(Boolean).length} critics` + (failedCritics.length ? `; no result from: ${failedCritics.join(', ')}` : ''))

Drop the claim that `aspects[i]` can be undefined. It cannot, because the filtered array is never longer than `aspects`.
